      "writtenOn": "2026-11-13T19:53:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can use the `--json` argument to the `review` command to do this.  Something like:\n```\nssh -p 29418 gerrit \\\n  gerrit review --json \u003cchange-number\u003e,\u003cpatchset-number\u003e \u003c\u003c\u0027JSON\u0027\n{\n  \"comments\": {\n    \"path/to/file.py\": [\n      {\n        \"in_reply_to\": \"ORIGINAL_COMMENT_UUID\",\n        \"message\": \"Reply text here.\",\n        \"unresolved\": false\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\nJSON\n```",
      "parentUuid": "ae017a4a_dd31dd6e",
